Technical report for both models:
  Vasileios Livathinos et al., "Advanced Layout Analysis Models for Docling"
  arXiv:2509.11720

Both revisions are Hugging Face commit shas, pinned in models.lock.json. They
are recorded as pinned commit identifiers so the exact bytes used for any
measurement in this repository can be identified; they assert no claim over the
repositories.

Weights are downloaded on demand by `scripts/fetch_models.py`, verified against
the recorded sha256, and are not committed to this repository.

On Linux the build resolves torch from PyTorch's CPU index (2.14.1+cpu) rather
than from PyPI, because the Linux wheels on PyPI are CUDA builds. No NVIDIA or
CUDA component is redistributed here, and none is required to run. See
pyproject.toml for the measurement reason and docs/runbook.md for the measured
effect on image size.

The exported ONNX files under artifacts/ are derived works of the weights above
and are produced by this project's `scripts/export_models.py`. Each carries its
own sha256 and a record of the parent weights' sha, the exporter, the opset and
the library versions used.

